# The repo's canonical text form is LF, enforced at checkout too: no smudge
# boundary between working tree and repo, so the byte-level gates (the frame
# tests compare exact terminal output, and `pack:check` compares file lists)
# see one form on every host. Windows is a supported platform for the TUI
# (PowerShell 7 + Windows Terminal), so this is not hypothetical.
#
# If a file class ever genuinely needs CRLF in the working tree (.bat/.cmd for
# cmd.exe), add a `*.bat text eol=crlf` override AFTER this line — the in-repo
# form stays LF; CRLF becomes checkout-time presentation only.
* text=auto eol=lf
